{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# MeCrab + Word2Vec: Training Japanese Word Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "**Date:** 2026-01-02  \n",
    "**Author:** COOLJAPAN OU (Team KitaSan)  \n",
    "**License:** MIT OR Apache-2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to train Word2Vec embeddings using MeCrab morphological analyzer and KizaMe CLI tools.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll follow the complete Word2Vec training pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Extract IPADIC vocabulary** with word_id mappings\n",
    "2. **Parse corpus** to word_id sequences using MeCrab\n",
    "3. **Train Word2Vec** using pure Rust implementation\n",
    "4. **Verify embeddings** and use in analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "# Install MeCrab Python package\n",
    "maturin develop --features python,parallel\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install IPADIC dictionary\n",
    "sudo apt install mecab-ipadic-utf8  # Ubuntu/Debian\n",
    "# brew install mecab-ipadic  # macOS\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install KizaMe CLI\n",
    "cargo install --path kizame\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import mecrab\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import tempfile\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"MeCrab version: {mecrab.version()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create working directory\n",
    "workdir = Path(\"./word2vec_training\")\n",
    "workdir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Working directory: {workdir.absolute()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Extract IPADIC Vocabulary\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we extract the complete vocabulary with word_id mappings from IPADIC dictionary:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "vocab_file = workdir / \"ipadic_vocab.txt\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract vocabulary using kizame\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [\"kizame\", \"dict\", \"dump\", \"-d\", \"/var/lib/mecab/dic/ipadic-utf8\", \"--vocab\"],\n",
    "    capture_output=True,\n",
    "    text=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    # Save vocabulary to file\n",
    "    with open(vocab_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        f.write(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Count lines\n",
    "    vocab_size = len(result.stdout.strip().split('\\n'))\n",
    "    print(f\"✓ Vocabulary extracted: {vocab_size:,} tokens\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Show sample\n",
    "    print(\"\\nSample vocabulary (first 5 entries):\")\n",
    "    for line in result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')[:5]:\n",
    "        word_id, feature = line.split('\\t', 1)\n",
    "        print(f\"  {word_id:6s} {feature[:60]}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Get max word_id\n",
    "    last_line = result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')[-1]\n",
    "    max_word_id = int(last_line.split('\\t')[0])\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nMax word_id: {max_word_id}\")\nelse:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error extracting vocabulary: {result.stderr}\")\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"Failed to extract vocabulary\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Prepare Sample Corpus\n",
    "\n",
    "For this demo, we'll use a small sample corpus. In production, you would use Japanese Wikipedia (~4GB).\n",
    "\n",
    "See [Word2Vec Training Guide](../kizame/WORD2VEC_TRAINING_GUIDE.md) for downloading and processing Wikipedia dumps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create sample corpus\n",
    "sample_corpus = \"\"\"\n",
    "東京は日本の首都です。\n",
    "東京には多くの人が住んでいます。\n",
    "東京タワーは有名な観光地です。\n",
    "日本の文化は素晴らしいです。\n",
    "京都も日本の古都として知られています。\n",
    "京都には多くの寺院があります。\n",
    "大阪は日本第二の都市です。\n",
    "大阪の食べ物は美味しいです。\n",
    "富士山は日本一高い山です。\n",
    "富士山は美しい景色で有名です。\n",
    "日本語は難しいですが面白い言語です。\n",
    "私は毎日日本語を勉強しています。\n",
    "今日は良い天気です。\n",
    "明日は雨が降るでしょう。\n",
    "週末は買い物に行きます。\n",
    "友達と映画を見ました。\n",
    "美味しいラーメンを食べました。\n",
    "公園で散歩をしました。\n",
    "図書館で本を読みました。\n",
    "音楽を聴くのが好きです。\n",
    "\"\"\".strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "corpus_file = workdir / \"sample_corpus.txt\"\n",
    "with open(corpus_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    f.write(sample_corpus)\n",
    "\n",
    "line_count = len(sample_corpus.split('\\n'))\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Sample corpus created: {line_count} sentences\")\n",
    "print(f\"  File: {corpus_file}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE: For production, download Wikipedia:\n",
    "# wget https://dumps.wikimedia.org/jawiki/latest/jawiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2\n",
    "# python3 -m wikiextractor.WikiExtractor -o wiki_text --json jawiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2\n",
    "# find wiki_text -name \"wiki_*\" -exec cat {} \\; | jq -r '.text' > jawiki_text.txt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Parse Corpus to word_id Sequences\n",
    "\n",
    "Convert text to word_id sequences for Word2Vec training:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize MeCrab\n",
    "m = mecrab.MeCrab()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Read corpus\n",
    "with open(corpus_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    corpus_lines = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Parsing {len(corpus_lines)} sentences...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Parse using Python API for demonstration\n",
    "# In production, use: kizame parse --wakati-word-id < input.txt > output.txt\n",
    "word_id_sequences = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, line in enumerate(corpus_lines, 1):\n",
    "    if i % 100 == 0:\n",
    "        print(f\"  Processed {i}/{len(corpus_lines)} sentences\", end='\\r')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Parse to get morphemes\n",
    "    # NOTE: Current Python API doesn't expose word_id directly\n",
    "    # We'll use CLI for this step\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Parsed {len(corpus_lines)} sentences\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Alternative: Use CLI (recommended for large corpora)\n",
    "corpus_ids_file = workdir / \"corpus_word_ids.txt\"\n",
    "\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [\"kizame\", \"parse\", \"--wakati-word-id\"],\n",
    "    input=sample_corpus,\n",
    "    capture_output=True,\n",
    "    text=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    with open(corpus_ids_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        f.write(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Show sample\n",
    "    print(\"\\nSample word_id sequences (first 3 lines):\")\n",
    "    for i, line in enumerate(result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')[:3], 1):\n",
    "        word_ids = line.split()\n",
    "        print(f\"  Sentence {i}: {' '.join(word_ids[:10])}... ({len(word_ids)} words)\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n✓ word_id sequences saved to {corpus_ids_file}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error parsing corpus: {result.stderr}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Train Word2Vec (Pure Rust)\n",
    "\n",
    "Train embeddings using KizaMe's built-in Word2Vec implementation:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "vectors_file = workdir / \"vectors.bin\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Training parameters\n",
    "params = {\n",
    "    \"size\": 50,        # Embedding dimension (small for demo)\n",
    "    \"window\": 5,       # Context window\n",
    "    \"negative\": 5,     # Negative samples\n",
    "    \"min_count\": 1,    # Minimum word frequency (low for small corpus)\n",
    "    \"sample\": 0.0001,  # Subsampling threshold\n",
    "    \"alpha\": 0.025,    # Initial learning rate\n",
    "    \"epochs\": 10,      # Training iterations (more for small corpus)\n",
    "    \"threads\": 4,      # Parallel threads\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training Word2Vec...\")\n",
    "print(f\"Parameters: {params}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nThis may take a few seconds...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train using CLI\n",
    "cmd = [\n",
    "    \"kizame\", \"vectors\", \"train\",\n",
    "    \"-i\", str(corpus_ids_file),\n",
    "    \"-o\", str(vectors_file),\n",
    "    \"-f\", \"mcv1\",\n",
    "    \"--max-word-id\", str(max_word_id),\n",
    "    \"--size\", str(params[\"size\"]),\n",
    "    \"--window\", str(params[\"window\"]),\n",
    "    \"--negative\", str(params[\"negative\"]),\n",
    "    \"--min-count\", str(params[\"min_count\"]),\n",
    "    \"--sample\", str(params[\"sample\"]),\n",
    "    \"--alpha\", str(params[\"alpha\"]),\n",
    "    \"--epochs\", str(params[\"epochs\"]),\n",
    "    \"--threads\", str(params[\"threads\"]),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "    print(result.stderr)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n✓ Embeddings saved to {vectors_file}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check file size\n",
    "    size_mb = vectors_file.stat().st_size / 1024 / 1024\n",
    "    print(f\"  File size: {size_mb:.2f} MB\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error training Word2Vec: {result.stderr}\")\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"Training failed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Verify Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Check the trained embeddings:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show vector info\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [\"kizame\", \"vectors\", \"info\", \"-v\", str(vectors_file)],\n",
    "    capture_output=True,\n",
    "    text=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: {result.stderr}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Use Embeddings in Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Parse text with word embeddings:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test_text = \"東京に行く\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Parse with vectors (using CLI)\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        \"kizame\", \"parse\",\n",
    "        \"--with-vector\",\n",
    "        \"-v\", str(vectors_file),\n",
    "        \"--with-ipa\"\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    input=test_text,\n",
    "    capture_output=True,\n",
    "    text=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    print(f\"Input: {test_text}\\n\")\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: {result.stderr}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: JSON-LD Output with Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Get structured output with embeddings:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "test_text = \"日本の文化\"\n",
    "\n",
    "result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        \"kizame\", \"parse\",\n",
    "        \"-O\", \"jsonld\",\n",
    "        \"--with-vector\",\n",
    "        \"-v\", str(vectors_file),\n",
    "        \"--with-ipa\"\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    input=test_text,\n",
    "    capture_output=True,\n",
    "    text=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    data = json.loads(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Input: {test_text}\\n\")\n",
    "    print(\"Morphemes with embeddings:\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for token in data.get(\"tokens\", []):\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n  Surface: {token['surface']}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  POS: {token.get('pos', 'N/A')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Reading: {token.get('reading', 'N/A')}\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if 'pronunciation' in token:\n",
    "            print(f\"  IPA: {token['pronunciation']}\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if 'embedding' in token:\n",
    "            emb = token['embedding']\n",
    "            if isinstance(emb, list):\n",
    "                preview = ', '.join(f\"{v:.3f}\" for v in emb[:5])\n",
    "                print(f\"  Embedding: [{preview}, ...] (dim={len(emb)})\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: {result.stderr}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Production Workflow Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "For production use with full Wikipedia corpus:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "# 1. Extract vocabulary\n",
    "kizame dict dump -d /var/lib/mecab/dic/ipadic-utf8 --vocab > vocab.txt\n",
    "MAX_WORD_ID=$(tail -1 vocab.txt | cut -f1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Download Wikipedia\n",
    "wget https://dumps.wikimedia.org/jawiki/latest/jawiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2\n",
    "wikiextractor -o wiki_text --json jawiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2\n",
    "find wiki_text -name \"wiki_*\" -exec cat {} \\; | jq -r '.text' > jawiki.txt\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Parse to word_id sequences (parallel)\n",
    "split -l 100000 jawiki.txt chunk_\n",
    "ls chunk_* | parallel -j8 'kizame parse --wakati-word-id < {} > {}.ids'\n",
    "cat chunk_*.ids > corpus_ids.txt\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Train Word2Vec (1-2 hours)\n",
    "kizame vectors train \\\n",
    "  -i corpus_ids.txt \\\n",
    "  -o vectors.bin \\\n",
    "  -f mcv1 \\\n",
    "  --max-word-id $MAX_WORD_ID \\\n",
    "  --size 100 \\\n",
    "  --window 5 \\\n",
    "  --negative 5 \\\n",
    "  --epochs 3 \\\n",
    "  --threads 8\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Deploy\n",
    "gzip vectors.bin\n",
    "scp vectors.bin.gz production:/opt/mecrab/data/\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "See [Word2Vec Training Guide](../kizame/WORD2VEC_TRAINING_GUIDE.md) for complete details."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "### Applications with Word Embeddings:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Semantic Similarity Search**\n",
    "   - Find similar words using cosine similarity\n",
    "   - Document clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Text Classification**\n",
    "   - Average word vectors for document representation\n",
    "   - Feed to ML models (SVM, Neural Networks)\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Word Analogies**\n",
    "   - \"東京\" - \"日本\" + \"フランス\" = \"パリ\"\n",
    "   - Vector arithmetic for semantic relationships\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Named Entity Recognition**\n",
    "   - Use embeddings as features for NER models\n",
    "\n",
    "### Enhanced Python API (Coming Soon):\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Future API with native vector support\n",
    "m = mecrab.MeCrab(\n",
    "    with_ipa=True,\n",
    "    vector_path=\"vectors.bin\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "result = m.parse_to_dict(\"東京に行く\")\n",
    "# => [\n",
    "#   {'surface': '東京', 'pos': '名詞', \n",
    "#    'ipa': '/toːkʲoː/',\n",
    "#    'embedding': array([0.1, -0.2, ...])},\n",
    "#   ...\n",
    "# ]\n",
    "```\n",
